WEBVTT

00:28:58.686 --> 00:29:01.764
Instead of asking questions
and listening to what candidates say,

00:29:01.788 --> 00:29:03.968
you get to observe what they do.

00:29:03.992 --> 00:29:06.173
And one of the workplaces
that's done it best

00:29:06.197 --> 00:29:08.738
happens to be in the great
state of Michigan,

00:29:08.762 --> 00:29:10.053
where I grew up.

00:29:11.164 --> 00:29:14.515
Richard Sheridan: I used to interview
the same way everybody else did,

00:29:14.539 --> 00:29:16.312
two people sitting across the table,

00:29:16.336 --> 00:29:18.502
lying to each other for a couple of hours

00:29:18.526 --> 00:29:21.820
and making a decision based on that.

00:29:22.613 --> 00:29:24.123
AG: Do you think it's that bad?

00:29:24.147 --> 00:29:26.543
RS: I think we're all trying
to puff each other up.

00:29:26.567 --> 00:29:29.368
None of us typically get
a very real impression,

00:29:29.392 --> 00:29:31.548
either of a candidate or of a company,